# MicrobatchPort-2b (rebased onto stack/prx-fixed + 1b + 3b; behaviour unchanged). MicrobatchPort-2: a row-split prompt chunk's DSA layers run their replicated front on each rank's own rows, its outputs
# shared instead of the normed rows (TF_GLM_PROMPT_OWN_FRONT=1 with TF_GLM_HC_SPLIT=1; default off until measured on
# the GB10 triangle). The non-indexer half of the recipe's tp4 0102 (the indexer's own-row top-k is OTS 0101's).
#
# - Why: before each DSA layer every rank swapped its own rows of the next normed input (8 KiB a row) so that every
#   rank could run DSA's replicated front on every row: q_a / kv_a and their RMSNorms, the indexer's key / weight
#   projection and gate. Here the glue keeps the normed rows on their owner (HcSplit.glue / glue_side share=False);
#   each rank runs that front on its own rows and shares b.ikr, b.igr (832 B a row) then b.qr, b.lat (4 KiB a row):
#   4.8 KiB a row instead of 8 KiB at the DSA layers' layer-end sites, and a third of those projections a rank.
# - own_front.py (new): applies, takes, dsa_block.
# - hcsplit.py: SplitSettings.own_front (TF_GLM_PROMPT_OWN_FRONT) in prompt_code; HcSplit.share / wait /
#   _swap_share (whole own shares, on the side stream with the overlap); glue / glue_side / _glue_rows share=.
# - forward.py: split_layer_steps runs own_front.dsa_block on DSA layers and keeps the normed rows before them;
#   dsa_rows(fronted=True) skips the index projections (already on every row).
# - microbatch.py: each half's DSA layers likewise (MicrobatchPort-1).
# - engine.py: the startup comparison's message.
# - Not taken: multi-prompt chunks, unsplit chunks, decode and verify windows, TF_GLM_KV_SHARD, TF_GLM_LATENT=0.
#
# Bits: bit-identical. Every kernel is the unchanged path's on the same row (projections, norms and writers keep rows
# apart); every rank writes its caches from the same shared bytes. Test: test_microbatch.py --own (6 own-front arms,
# with and without halving, p2p and all-gather, overlap 0 / 1 / 2, x 3 delay profiles: every output and cache
# bit-identical to the unchanged split; each arm ran the own-row front on every DSA layer and sent fewer bytes);
# mutants own-* (mutants_microbatch.py). Applies on top of MicrobatchPort-1 and -3.
#
# Ported from the GLM-5.3 recipe's tp4 patch 0102 (Mia's AI Lab, Apache-2.0); design credit drowzeys
